Original license reproduced in LICENSE. No Calango AGPL code imported. Source file history checked for initial classifier/model slice; broader attribution and legal gate remain open (Nexus #74). No release or relicensing implied. Future ports must update this inventory and preserve all required notices.

Second extraction from the same Nexus commit:
- providers/spec/* and contract goldens: internal/core/provider/spec/*; AGY helper directory injected by host rather than resolving a Nexus path.
- runtime/discovery.go, executable.go and executable_test.go: selected runtime helpers; no process execution or secret store copied.
- coordination/request.go: independent envelope, validation, semantic equality/ID and limits from internal/nexus/runner/coordination.go; no MissionRunner copied.
- capacity/*: pure threshold, transition and fingerprint logic, types and tests from internal/nexus/capacitymonitor/{types,state,state_test}.go.
- routing/reason.go: typed switch reason from internal/nexus/runtime_routing.go; routing/fallback.go adds a host-authorized conservative gate, not a transactional handoff.
- hud/types.go and primary.go: read-only DTOs and primary selection from internal/nexus/hud_projection.go; cost enum fields represented by strings.
- providers/parsers/{claude,gemini}: JSON normalization from respective usage_live.go; no auth or HTTP requests copied.
New tests exercise local primitives. No real user credentials or session records copied. Broader legal and integration gates remain open.

Additional extraction from Nexus source commit above:
- providers/parsers/codex/usage.go: app-server quota response mapping from internal/core/provider/adapters/codex/app_server_usage.go and codex.go, with stricter identity and missing-value gates. Synthetic tests; no upstream personal data copied.
- providers/contract.go: provider-neutral host ports adapted from internal/core/provider/provider.go. No product runtime or credentials copied.
